ged so much the books don't  recognize me as human when I leave they  don't try to stop me as I reach the edge  of the cavern a blinding light envelops  me I've made it to freedom of a sort  whatever they are they don't mind when I  hitch a ride Swit stone pillars  punctuate an endless sea of white fog I  feel like a small bird navigating a  petrified forest the only living things  I see are the other bogs in some sort of  floating creature good god what is this  thing  I've got to take a closer look yes  finally or am I not to be so lucky as we  make our way towards the quarry loosens  my binds and begins to speak I ask him  first why the darkness in the distance  is not returned he tells me it was never  there to begin with only an illusion to  prevent prey from wandering too far from  the jelly as a walled structure comes  into view I cry out his glare silences  me I notice upon entry that the door is  made of bones and so are the tents save  a brittle layer of what looks like skin  stretched over them as if anticipating  my questions he holds up a small brick  and explains that his form from a  combination of ground bone dust and glue  made from boiled ligaments his own  remains and those of others fished out  of the black jelly after the bugs are  fed on their flyff assume find myself in  the presence of their leader who has  suffered more mutation than any of us he  spoke of the shafts to the surface world  to which we can never return or rather  not with any permanence raids were  actually quite frequent though it seemed  only the bugs could open the tunnels  I rest prepare my mind and begin to a  sad
 

